From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:30:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: emulate sampler min/max reduction before Apple10

Apple's Metal Feature Set Tables restrict "Sampler minimum and maximum
reduction" (MTLSamplerDescriptor.reductionMode) to Apple10; on Apple7 Metal
validation aborts with "Use of minimum or maximum reductionMode requires
device support". VK_EXT_sampler_filter_minmax / samplerFilterMinmax /
filterMinmaxSingleComponentFormats (vkd3d-proton requires them for Tiled
Resources Tier 2, hence feature level 12_0) were Apple10-only.

Keep the native path on Apple10. Before it, samplers with a min/max
reduction become point samplers and carry their reduction and min/mag/mip
filters in the descriptor's spare two bytes (sampler_filter_flags). A NIR
pass (when samplerFilterMinmax is enabled, part of the shader key) branches
on those flags for non-shadow float samples: it computes and clamps lambda,
picks the magnification or minification filter and the mip levels, and
reduces per component only the texels with a non-zero bilinear/trilinear
weight, each fetched at its exact center through the application's sampler
(address modes, border colors, array layers and swizzles stay the view's
and sampler's). The footprint fetch is emitted once per texture type as a
non-inlined MSL helper to keep pipeline compile times down (gamescope's 30
pipelines: 20.6 s without, 28.6 s with the feature enabled). Sparse samples
AND the residency of the contributing texels.

Approximations: anisotropy is ignored for min/max (allowed); cube maps
sample face interiors exactly, reproject seam texels onto the neighboring
face and use the nearest texels at corners.
---
